# Line endings are part of this repository's content, not a local detail.
#
# `experiment.hash_task` hashes each task's files byte-for-byte, and a
# published result is only comparable to another one carrying the same
# task hashes. With `core.autocrlf=true` — the Windows default — a
# checkout rewrites those files to CRLF, so the same frozen task hashes
# differently on Windows than on Linux and two runs of "the identical
# protocol" silently disagree about what they measured.
#
# Pinning LF makes a checkout byte-identical on every platform, which is
# what "frozen tasks" has to mean for the hashes to be worth recording.
#
# (`git apply` reconciles an LF patch against a CRLF file on its own, so
# the inner loop's patch tool is not affected by this — see
# tests/test_tools.py. The hashing is the reason.)

* text=auto eol=lf

# Frozen, content-hashed evaluation material and the harnesses measured
# against it. Never platform-converted.
eval/** text eol=lf
benchmarks/** text eol=lf
agents/** text eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF or they will not run under bash.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Content git should not rewrite.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
uv.lock text eol=lf
